## Layout

| Area | Where |
|---|---|
| Schema / migrate | `Data/PalaceDb.cs` |
| Durable catalog path | `Helpers/CatalogStore.cs` (default `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Palace\catalog\palace.db` outside MSIX Packages; pointer `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Palace\catalog-root.txt` survives `winapp unregister`; LocalSettings `CatalogRootPath` / `CatalogAccessToken` are a cache only. Startup migrates a non-empty LocalState `palace.db` into the durable root via `SnapshotDatabase` (SQLite backup API, temp file then rename, never overwrites) after a raw copy to `<root>\backups\localstate-premigrate-*`. If both exist, the durable one opens and LocalState is copied to `backups\localstate-unmerged-*`. Folder switch uses `TryCopyActiveCatalogTo` and never overwrites a catalog already in the target. Settings `TxtCatalogPath` / `BtnPickCatalogFolder` / `BtnResetCatalogFolder` / `BtnExportCatalogCopy`. **Unregister wipes LocalState** — never treat package LocalState as the only copy of user data.) |
| Tag export / import | `Helpers/TagPortable.cs` + `CatalogService.ExportTagsJsonAsync` / `ImportTagsJsonAsync` (schema `palace-tags/1`; upsert by name; cycle-safe parents/implicits; does not wipe unrelated tags). Settings `BtnExportTags` / `BtnImportTags`. Tags stay **global**. |
| Catalog queries | `Services/CatalogService.cs` + partials `CatalogService.{Sources,Assets,Tags,TagAssignments,Organize,Rooms,Search}.cs` |
| Scan / index | `Services/ScanService.cs` |
| Thumbs | `Services/ThumbnailService.cs` |
| Open hydrate | `Services/HydrationService.cs` |
| Cloud accounts + OAuth | `Services/CloudAccountService.cs`, `Services/Cloud/` |
| Library mosaic | `ViewModels/LibraryViewModel.cs` + partials `LibraryViewModel.{Selection,Scan,Filters,Tagging,Mosaic,Folders,Preview,Overlay,FileActions,Organize}.cs`, `Pages/LibraryPage.xaml` |
| Asset → tile | `Helpers/AssetItemMapper.cs` (not ad-hoc `ToItem` probes) |
| UI thread hops | `Helpers/UiDispatch.cs` |
| Errors / crash logging | `Helpers/ErrorReporter.cs`, `Helpers/ErrorLog.cs`, `Helpers/ErrorThrottle.cs` |
| Load side-effect gate | `Helpers/LoadGate.cs` (`using Begin()` so swallowed `LoadAsync` failures always clear; MainPage / Settings project + settings writes) |
| On-Demand detect | `Helpers/CloudFile.cs` |
| Scan original-read policy | `Helpers/ScanContent.cs` (`MayReadOriginal` / `MayGenerateScanThumbnail`) |
| Thumb cache names | `Helpers/ThumbFileName.cs` |
| Optional media cache | `Helpers/MediaCache.cs` (opt-in Settings; LocalSettings `MediaCacheEnabled` / `MediaCacheMaxMb` / `MediaCacheRootPath` / `MediaCacheAccessToken`; default off — LocalFolder `thumbs/` still works without a size cap. When on: max size LRU eviction under `<root>/thumbs` + future `<root>/preview`, optional FolderPicker + FutureAccessList; refuse watched sources (**all projects**) and On-Demand/cloud roots; `IsAllowedSource` blocks Add folder under the active cache root. `EnsureRoots` falls back to LocalFolder when the custom drive is missing (startup / `ApplyMediaCacheRoot` must not throw). Settings `TglMediaCache` / `SldMediaCacheMaxMb` / `TxtMediaCacheMaxMb` / `TxtMediaCacheUsage` / `TxtMediaCachePath` / `BtnPickCacheFolder` / `BtnResetCacheFolder` / `BtnClearCache`. `AppServices.ApplyMediaCacheRoot` re-points `ThumbnailService`; missing JPEGs regenerate lazily. Never beside sources; never recall On-Demand to fill. Magick/PSD/HDR present can use `preview/` later.) |
| Overlay / mosaic media | `Helpers/GalleryMedia.cs` |
| Overlay GIF scrub | `Helpers/GifFrames.cs` (count / wrap index / transparent composite + one-pass `TryRenderAll` cache + overflow-safe `FitsCacheBudget` 256 MB / 2048 frames + `FitsFramePixels` on descriptor fw×fh + cancel token + play clock after cache; `PassesGifSliderArrows` so overlay Left/Right do not steal `SldGifFrame` / `SldGalleryWindowGifFrame`; never On-Demand) |
| Overlay scale / HDR probe | `Helpers/GalleryScale.cs` (1:1/Fit/Fill, Space/Esc, `DragPan` / pinch), `Helpers/HdrFile.cs`, `Helpers/HdrColor.cs`, `Helpers/HdrPixels.cs`, `Helpers/GalleryPresent.cs` |
| Overlay / GalleryWindow backdrop | Overlay: `GalleryOverlayBackdropBrush` + Smoke (`GrdGalleryBackdrop`). GalleryWindow: `DesktopAcrylicBackdrop` + one 0.28 Smoke (no root Smoke fill, no stacked in-app acrylic) |
| HDR peak override | `Helpers/GalleryPeak.cs` (Settings `TglHdrPeakOverride` / `SldHdrPeakNits`, LocalSettings `HdrPeakOverrideEnabled` / `HdrPeakOverrideNits`; present reads `PresentOverrideNits`) |
| Gallery Details / Info / Loop chrome | `Helpers/GalleryChrome.cs` (overlay / GalleryWindow `ShowDetails` / `ShowImageInfo` / `LoopVideo`; LocalSettings `GalleryShowDetails` / `GalleryShowImageInfo` / `GalleryLoopVideo`; first-run default on, then persist; `BtnGalleryDetails` / `BtnGalleryWindowDetails` / `BtnGalleryImageInfo` / `BtnGalleryWindowImageInfo` / `BtnGalleryLoop` / `BtnGalleryWindowLoop`; `MediaPlayer.IsLoopingEnabled`. Top chrome buttons sit on an opaque `SolidBackgroundFillColorSecondaryBrush` bar so icon+text stay readable on white stills) |
| Video mosaic poster from frame | `Helpers/VideoMosaicThumb.cs` + `Services/VideoFrameThumb.cs` (overlay / GalleryWindow `BtnGallerySetThumb` / `BtnGalleryWindowSetThumb`, Fluent `Image` + “Set thumb”; visible only for playable local MediaPlayer video — hide online-only / API, never hydrate for a poster; capture at `PlaybackSession.Position` via `MediaComposition.GetThumbnailAsync`, scale to `ThumbnailService.MaxSide`, write bare-hash JPEG under thumb cache via `CacheScaledJpegAsync`, refresh `AssetItem.ThumbPath` / `ThumbImage` with `IgnoreImageCache`; no Magick / Win2D) |
| Glass wallpaper | `Helpers/ShellChrome.cs` (full-window Page / Nav / content Transparent; pane `AcrylicInAppFillColorDefaultBrush`; never `SolidBackgroundFillColorBase` sheet), `Helpers/ShellBackground.cs` (parse/apply, LocalSettings `ShellWallpaperPath` / `ShellDarkness` / `ShellBlur` / `ShellTintEnabled` / `ShellTintColor`), `Helpers/ShellBackdrop.cs` (theme gradient + Acrylic + dim + tint behind chrome). Settings `BtnPickWallpaper` / `BtnClearWallpaper` / `SldShellDarkness` / `SldShellBlur` / `TglShellTint` / `PkrShellTint`. Store copies use unique `shell-wallpaper-*` names; Settings `TxtShellWallpaper` shows the user's chosen file name (`ShellBackground.WallpaperName`, LocalSettings `ShellWallpaperName`), not the generated store name; `ReleaseDisplay` before replace so BitmapImage does not lock the file; failed copy calls `RestoreDisplay` (`Changed` without bumping `WallpaperEpoch`) and deletes the unused `shell-wallpaper-*` dest. `ReleaseDisplay` sets `DisplayHeld` so theme `Refresh` / slider `Changed` cannot re-bind the previous file (and lock it) during copy; `ShouldBindWallpaper` is false until `RestoreDisplay` or `Apply` with a path/`reloadWallpaper`. Resident wallpaper `BitmapImage` sets physical `DecodePixelWidth` (`ShellBackground.WallpaperDecodeWidth` 2560) **before** `UriSource` — the Uri constructor starts a native decode and ignores a later cap. `WallpaperEpoch` increments only on path change or `reloadWallpaper: true` — darkness/blur/tint sliders must not re-decode the image. `Apply(..., reloadWallpaper: true)` still fires `Changed` on the same path. Default gradient / glass tint / dim follow Light vs Dark (`IsLightChrome` / `DimOpacity`). Full-window Page / Frame / NavigationView / content fills are Transparent (`Helpers/ShellChrome.cs`) so wallpaper shows through nav, panes, and pages — do not cover with `SolidBackgroundFillColorBase` / `ApplicationPageBackgroundThemeBrush` or stacked `AcrylicInAppFillColorDefaultBrush`. Nav pane uses `AcrylicInAppFillColorDefaultBrush` (`PaneBackground`); override `NavigationViewContentBackground` to Transparent. Cards / tiles keep `CardBackgroundFillColorDefaultBrush` / ThemeResource. Do not hardcode pane/tile brushes. No Win2D. |
| HDR present raster / coalesce / measure size | `Helpers/HdrRasterize.cs` (`HdrRasterize`, `HdrHalfBuffer`), `Helpers/HdrPresentCoalescer.cs`, `GalleryPresent.MeasureDecodeSize`; callers `Services/HdrSwapchainPresenter.cs`, `Services/HdrWicDecode.cs`, `Controls/GalleryStillSurface.xaml.cs` |
| HDR AVIF present (libavif) | `Services/HdrAvifDecode.cs` (`Starward.Codec` `avif.dll`); WIC is fallback only |
| HDR JXR present (WIC COM float) | `Helpers/WicNative.cs` flattened IUnknown vtables + `Services/HdrWicDecode.cs` unpack native float/half/`1010102XR` in `HdrPixels`, box-scale scRGB (do not WIC-scale HDR formats — scaler throws → SDR preview); packaged JXR: native float/half `CopyPixels` (filename / handle / memory) first; then `CoCreate` / `DllGetClassObject(CLSID_WICWmpDecoder)` + `Initialize` (`wmp`) when the factory catalog omits HD Photo; then `BitmapDecoder.CreateAsync(stream)` (**no** decoder ID) and QI `IWinRTObject.ThisPtr` → `IWICBitmapDecoder` / frame via `TypedUniqueFromIUnknown` (`GetUniqueObjectForIUnknown`, not cached `GetTypedObjectForIUnknown`) for float `CopyPixels`; RAS always runs when QI lacks float — `Seek(0)` then `CreateStreamOverRandomAccessStream` + `CreateDecoderFromStream` (`rasStream` / `rasDecoder`); chain prior QI/unorm with RAS via `WicDecoderOpen.Join` (RAS must not hide QI); **packaged float HDR JXR wall** (Main-Desktop `9d57a68`): Display `wmp 80004002; qi 80004002; rasDecoder 80004005` — CoCreate/DllGetClassObject `CLSID_WICWmpDecoder` and WinRT→WIC QI are both `E_NOINTERFACE`; factory `CreateDecoderFromStream` is `E_FAIL`. WinRT `BitmapPixelFormat` has **no float** (Rgba16/Rgba8/Bgra8 unorm only — MS docs: fidelity loss). `BitmapImage` SDR of Captures JXR is `UriSource` → same SDR imaging pipeline (`GalleryStillSurface.ToStillImage`), not float scRGB. Stamp `packaged` via `IsPackagedNoFloatWall` / `MarkPackagedWall`. **Do not** retry more CLSIDs. Float present needs a shipped decoder (jxrlib / Magick packaging spike) or an unpackaged host; until then keep SDR preview + unorm reject. AVIF scRGB via libavif is unaffected; WinRT `Rgba16`/`Rgba8`/`Bgra8` unorm **clamps HDR** (`JxrWinrtClampsHdr`) — do **not** present (`unorm`); fix `ISoftwareBitmapNative` IID `94BC8415-…` (not `94c952b4-…`); do **not** `GetIUnknownForObject` for QI (fake `80004002`); do **not** `CreateDecoder(GUID_ContainerFormatWmp)` (`0x88982F50`), do **not** `CoCreate(CLSID_WICWmpDecoder)` or `CreateAsync(JpegXrDecoderId)`; `LastWicError` stamps `CreateAsync` / `qi` / `ras` / `unorm` + HRESULT on Overlay `Display:`; not Magick / libjxl |
| Radiance RGBE | `Helpers/RadianceFile.cs` (C#; no Magick) |
| JXL / JXR / PSD / DDS headers | `Helpers/StillFormats.cs` (JXL `ImageMetadata` + container `colr` CICP; HDR is PQ/HLG only; P3 is primaries 11; size-only is not HDR. JXR HDR is Annex A `PIXEL_FORMAT` 0xBC01 float/half/`1010102XR` GUID → `HdrKind.HdrJxr`; size is 0xBC80/0xBC81 — 0xBC82/83 are FLOAT DPI, not pixels) |
| Library folder groups | `Helpers/FolderGroups.cs` |
| Library mosaic rows | `Helpers/MosaicRows.cs` (compact header slots vs justified tiles), `Helpers/JustifiedMosaicLayout.cs` |
| Library tag browse mosaic | `Helpers/TagBrowseMosaic.cs` (`Flatten`; Library `TreTagsBrowse` / `BrowseTags`), `Helpers/ChipWrap.cs` / `ChipWrapLayout` (WASDK 2.4 has no public `WrapLayout`) |
| Library select mode | `Helpers/SelectMode.cs` (`ClickTogglesTile` → `Multiple` vs `Single`, never Extended; `EnterFromHold` press-and-hold / click-and-hold on a mosaic tile enters select mode and selects that tile without opening overlay; `Summary` count text, `ShowBatchTagCta`; `TglSelectMode` / `TxtSelectionCount` / `BtnTagSelected` / `CmbMosaicSort` in the same cluster) |
| Mosaic sort | `Helpers/MosaicSortOrder.cs` (`MosaicSort` enum → allowlisted `ORDER BY`; `ShouldApplyIndex` ignores ComboBox `-1`; `CmbMosaicSort` / `CmbTagMosaicSort` OneWay + armed SelectionChanged; LocalSettings `MosaicSort_{projectId}`; Library `Loaded` `ReloadMosaicSortAsync`) |
| Multi-delete prune | `Helpers/MosaicDelete.cs` (in-place mosaic/`_allAssets` prune + empty folder-header strip; watcher directory Created/Renamed only — Renamed orphans old prefix then `ScanDirectoryAsync` on new; `LooksLikeDeletedDirectory` uses catalog ext so `shots.backup` / `.cache` still orphan-clean; `ChunkIds` for batched `DeleteAssetsAsync` — materialize FTS rowids before `DeleteFtsRow`; Library `DeleteFilesAsync` + `WatcherService.SuppressNotifications`) |
| Shortcut cheatsheet | `Helpers/ShortcutCheatsheet.cs` (Settings → About; `LstShortcuts` / `TxtShortcut*`; keep `TxtAppVersion` / `TxtInfancyNote`) |
| Mosaic range select | `Helpers/RangeSelect.cs` (contiguous first→last, skip headers; touch hold then `CapturePointer`; hit-test uses window coords via `ToWindowPoint`; live drag skips `LoadPreviewAsync`; `TglTagSelectMode` / `TxtTagSelectionCount` on Tags) |
| Cloud source paths | `Helpers/CloudSourcePath.cs` |
| Room icon ids | `Helpers/RoomIcons.cs` |
| Tags mosaic groups | `Helpers/TagMosaicGroups.cs` (longest path under the selected root, then Priority then name) |
| Tag name lists | `Helpers/TagNameList.cs` |
| Tag filter sets | `Helpers/TagFilter.cs` |
| Tag board / assign panel | `Helpers/TagPanelBuilder.cs` (`BuildBoard` pins All / Uncategorized / Starred, then user groups; Uncategorized keeps `BtnTagGroup_Ungrouped`) |
| Tag board expand | `Helpers/TagBoardExpand.cs` (create/select opens the row that shows the tag) |
| Tag sibling order | `Helpers/TagSiblings.cs` |
| Tag group destinations | `Helpers/TagGroups.cs` |
| Tag A–Z index | `Helpers/TagAlphaIndex.cs` (letter buckets; Tags board chips wrap under each header) |
| Tag children mosaic | `Pages/TagsPage.xaml` (`RepTagChildren` `WrapLayout` chips; keep `BtnTagChip_*`) |
| Tag board chip chrome | `Helpers/TagChipChrome.cs` (fill background, width from name; `TagColor.ChipFill` / `ChipInk`) |
| Tag rename apply | `Helpers/TagSelection.cs` |
| Recent tags | `Helpers/RecentTags.cs` |
| Preview generation fields | `Helpers/GenerationFields.cs` (empty Extract/catalog replaces prior Prompt/Model; hide Generation when `HasAny` is false) |
| Preview notes persist | `Helpers/PreviewPersist.cs` (`ClearPreview` / overlay apply must not write notes or rating onto `SelectedAsset`) |
| Fluent enum parse | `Helpers/FluentGlyph.cs` (XAML only) |
| UI tests | `ui-tests.ps1` (`winapp ui`, AutomationIds; assert `Txt*` / `Btn*` / `Grd*` elements — a plain `Border` such as `BrdGalleryOverlayInfo` / `BrdGalleryImageInfo` has no automation peer, so UIA cannot see it; assert the text inside instead). Histogram: assert `TxtGalleryWindowHistogram` / `TxtGalleryWindowInfoHistogram` / `TxtGalleryOverlayHistogram` when an HDR still is presented; do not require them on SDR-only fixtures. Overlay scale: assert `BtnGalleryScaleActual` / `BtnGalleryScaleFit` / `BtnGalleryScaleFill` on the open overlay (top chrome with Info / Details, not inside the Details bar). HDR chip: assert `IcnGalleryOverlayHdr` / `IcnGalleryWindowHdr` / mosaic `IcnHdrBadge_*` the same way (Fluent `Hdr` Regular Size24 + face `HDR` on Accent); skip on SDR-only fixtures. || App version | `Helpers/AppVersion.cs` (identity + Debug/Release + milestone; About keeps `TxtAppVersion` above the shortcut list) |
